# Hillman Minx Series V four-door saloon, 1956-1967.
#
# The Series I-V Minx, represented by the Series V the pack photographs. The
# range ran 1956-67 and the later Series V/VI are the best-evidenced cars;
# the earlier series are not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillman_Minx
#
# Dimensions 4.115 x 1.543 x 1.511 m, wheelbase 2.438 m (Series IIIC).
#
# Shape reference: NO true side profile exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter about 35 degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it
# and the other views within the published dimensions. The pack photographs
# a IIIA and a Series V. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period chart was found. Black, white, red and blue
# are plain names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 130 km/h. Comfort 55/265, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 1956 intro, retires staggered 1982-1985.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/hillman-minx-series.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/hillman-minx-series.dae. References:
# citycars/references/hillman-minx-series/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true rear view; the fins and lamp housings
# are simplified. The IIIA's grille and roof rack were not copied, and the other
# series are not separately represented. At 128 px the Series V grille, lamps
# and finned tail read as a Series V Minx.


obj=citycar
name=HillmanMinxSeries(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=1956
intro_month=1
retire_year=1985
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=55
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=265

Image[E]=./images/hillman-minx-series-black_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/hillman-minx-series-black_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/hillman-minx-series-black_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/hillman-minx-series-black_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/hillman-minx-series-black_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/hillman-minx-series-black_NW.0.0,12,10
